R"VG(
# industrial3.vg (H-04's second pass): the newspaper's columns: the small items of a town's week, each composed of its parts (who did
# what, where, at what price in their coin) and the town's own words: its market's crops, its works' craft, its quarters and landmark,
# its feast. One of a kind a paper (`once`).

ind.col
  (once 2) {ind.market}
  (once 1.5) {ind.council}
  (once 1.2) {ind.court}
  (once) {ind.lost}
  (once 1.2) {ind.reader}
  (once) {ind.weather}
  (once coast=1) {ind.ships}
  (once inv.railway=1) {ind.rail}
  (once) {ind.hall}
  (once) {ind.sports}
  (once) {ind.faith}
  (once) {ind.school}
  (once) {ind.works}
  (once) {ind.oddity}
  (once) {ind.health}
  (once stage>=1 2) {ind.late}
  (once) {ind.festival}

# ---- the market ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ind.market
  {ind.mkt.lead} {crop} at {n} {smallcoin} the {ind.mkt.unit}, {fruit} {ind.mkt.trend}, and {veg} {ind.mkt.trend2}.
  {ind.mkt.lead} the {crop} {ind.mkt.verb}, and {ind.mkt.other}.
  {ind.mkt.lead} {ind.mkt.other}; the {crop}, {ind.mkt.crop2}.
ind.mkt.lead
  At the {$home} market this week:
  The market:
  Prices at {town.open} of {$home}:
  From the corn exchange:
  Market day at {$home}:
  The week's prices:
