  changed the story twice
  been asleep at the time
  turned out to be the accused's cousin

# ---- lost, found and missing ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ind.lost
  Lost, between {ind.lost.a} and {ind.lost.b}: {ind.lost.what}. {ind.lost.reward}
  Found, near {ind.lost.a}: {ind.lost.what}. The owner may claim it at {ind.claim.at}.
ind.claim.at
  the office of this paper
  the police house
  {holyplace}
  the inn by the market
  the school, from the caretaker
  the bakery, where it is in the way
ind.lost.a
  the station
  the market
  the bridge
  {holyplace}
  the school
  the old wall
ind.lost.b
  the square
  the river
  the mill
  the north gate
  the inn
  the burying ground
ind.lost.what
  a {colour.any} {garment.n}, much mended
  a {beast} answering to its dinner
  a purse with {n} {coin} in it
  a child's boot, of no value but to the owner
  a ledger, much needed
  a pair of spectacles in a {colour.any} case
  {tool}, with the owner's mark on the handle
  a basket of {fruit}
ind.lost.reward
  A reward is offered.
  No questions asked.
  Reward: {n} {smallcoin}, and thanks.
  The finder will be blessed.

# ---- the readers --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ind.reader
  A reader {ind.rd.verb} {ind.rd.topic}.
  A reader {ind.rd.verb} {ind.rd.topic}; {ind.rd.reply}.
  {ind.rd.signed} {ind.rd.verb} {ind.rd.topic}.
ind.rd.verb
  writes to complain of
  asks what is to be done about
  writes in praise of
  wishes to know who is responsible for
  has written for the fourth time about
ind.rd.topic
  the smell of the {craft} works
  the price of {food}
  the {bird} on the roof of {holyplace}
  the noise of {instrument} from the hall after midnight
  the state of {streets.of}
  the young people and their {ind.sport}
  the {pest} in the granaries
  the bells on a feast day
  the {herd} driven through {town.open} on market days
  the new lamps, which light everything but the street
  the cost of a burial at {deadplace}
ind.rd.reply
  this paper agrees, and has said so before
  the council has been sent a copy
  we print the letter as it came
  the reader may be assured that we have looked into it, and found the reader right
ind.rd.signed
  A ratepayer of long standing
  A mother of six
  An old subscriber
  One who remembers better days

# ---- the weather -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ind.weather
  The weather: {weather.now}, {ind.wx.tail}.
  The week's weather was {weather.now} and {ind.wx.tail2}.
ind.wx.tail
  and more of it promised
  with worse in the hills
  clearing by the rest day, the almanac says
  and the almanac wrong again
ind.wx.tail2
  the gutters of {$home} have not been equal to it
  the {herd} have been brought in
  the {crop} in the low fields has suffered
  the old people say they have known worse

# ---- the ships, the railway -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ind.ships
  In harbour this week: {n} boats from the coast with {fish} and {fruit}; sailed: {n}, with {ind.ship.cargo}.
  The harbour master reports {ind.ship.news}.
ind.ship.cargo
  {crop} for {dest}
  {craft} goods for the south
  {vessel} and salt
  passengers and their {herd}
ind.ship.news
  a boat overdue from the north with {fish}, and the families waiting at the quay
  a quiet week, and the gulls fat on {fish}
  the new lights on the mole lit for the first time, with {fuel}
  a whale in the bay, which drew more of the town than {feast.custom}

ind.rail
  The {ind.rail.time} train from {$home} will run late until {ind.rail.why}.
  Passengers are reminded that the {ind.rail.time} train no longer stops at {$home} {ind.rail.unless}.
ind.rail.time
  morning
  noon
  evening
  night
ind.rail.why
  the line is mended
  the bridge is mended
  the flood goes down
  the new engine comes
  the snow is cleared from the cutting

